<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhofar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhofar is the southern governorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, with its capital at Salalah. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monsoon">monsoon</a>-watered hills are the classic home of frankincense, traded since antiquity through ports such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumhuram">Sumhuram</a> (Khor Rori). Ruled at times by Hadramawt and by Yemeni dynasties such as the Rasulids, it passed to the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> in the 19th century, and from 1963 to 1976 it was the scene of the Dhofar Rebellion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhofar.jpg" alt="Dhofar" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhofar_in_Oman_2016.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Saba also lay on the caravan routes that carried frankincense and myrrh, gathered from trees in Hadramawt, <b>Dhofar</b> and the Horn of Africa, north through western Arabia to Gaza and the Mediterranean and to Mesopotamia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-saba">Kingdom of Saba · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>It provided bases and supplies to the guerrillas of the <b>Dhofar</b> rebellion against the Sultanate of Oman until the rebellion was defeated in the mid-1970s, and it backed the leftist National Democratic Front in North Yemen.</blockquote><a href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 16th century Sultan Badr Abu Tuwayriq expanded Kathiri rule across Hadramawt and into <b>Dhofar</b>, using firearms and troops obtained through Ottoman contacts.</blockquote><a href="/state/kathiri-sultanate">Kathiri Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>Its wealth came from frankincense, gathered in <b>Dhofar</b> where Hadramawt founded the port of Sumhuram (Khor Rori), and shipped through Qana on the Indian Ocean coast, a port described in the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Kingdom of Hadramawt</a></li><li><blockquote>Under al-Muzaffar Yusuf, who reigned for 45 years and took <b>Dhofar</b> in 1279, the state reached from Mecca's borders to Dhofar.</blockquote><a href="/state/rasulid-dynasty">Rasulid dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Oil exports began in 1967 but development stayed slow while the <b>Dhofar</b> rebellion grew.</blockquote><a href="/state/sultanate-of-muscat-and-oman">Sultanate of Muscat and Oman</a></li></ul></section>
